'''Leoz''' was a [[Nikto]] [[pirate]] in [[Kragan Gorr]]'s [[Warbird gang]].

==Biography==
[[File:Leoz-SynarasScore.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Leoz wearing stormtrooper armor]]
Leoz<ref name="Kaz's Curse">{{Resistance|Kaz's Curse}}</ref> was a [[Gender|male]]<ref name="Databank" /> [[Nikto]] [[pirate]] who was a member of the [[Warbird gang]].<ref name="Kaz's Curse" /> Leoz stood behind the leader of the Warbird gang, [[Kragan Gorr]], when the [[Quarren]] talked to their [[First Order]] superiors after a failed [[Attack on the Colossus|attack]] on the ''[[Colossus]]''.<ref name="The Triple Dark" /> Later, Leoz took part in a [[Raid on the Colossus|second raid]] on the refueling station. During the attack, he was stealing a small crate when the [[Technician|mechanic]] [[Tamara Ryvora]] rammed a [[Repulsorlift|repulsor]] carrier into him, sending him crashing into the wall. Ryvora left him sprawled across the floor as residents of the ''Colossus'' came to seize the contents of the carrier.<ref name="Synara's Score" /> After the pirates were betrayed by the First Order, Leoz was present when the fellow pirate [[Valik]] announced she had intercepted an encoded transmission sent from the ''Colossus'', which she brought to Gorr. The message turned out to be a transmission sent to the [[Resistance]] by [[Kazuda Xiono]], who was calling for help.<ref name="Descent">{{Resistance|Descent (episode)}}</ref>

During the [[Skirmish over D'Qar|skirmish]] over [[D'Qar]], Leoz and the rest of the crew were scared as the ''[[Galleon]]'' have nearly crash-landed on the hangar as they got the [[coaxium]].<ref name="A Quick Salvage Run">{{Resistance|A Quick Salvage Run}}</ref> Leoz heard from Drell that Doza had a "real mess on his hands," as Kragan asserted was an opportunity for the gang.<ref name="Hunt on Celsor 3">{{Resistance|Hunt on Celsor 3}}</ref> Later, after the Warbirds had allied with the ''Colossus'' and began to stay on the refueling station, Leoz placed a curse on Xiono after being angered by the [[pilot]]'s winning streak on a [[gambling]] game Xiono had been invited to play because the pirates thought he would be easy pickings. Xiono later got back at Leoz by giving him a [[Kaz's talisman|talisman]] he had acquired from [[Mika Grey]], which he claimed was cursed.<ref name="Kaz's Curse" />

==Personality and traits==
Leoz had orange skin, one [[Color|blue]] [[eye]], the other being covered with an eye patch. He was considered a sore loser, willing to place alleged curses on people who had defeated him in games of chance. Leoz was also superstitious, using a pair of dice he considered good luck while gambling as well as believing in curses.<ref name="Databank" />

==Equipment==
Leoz wore part of a [[stormtrooper]] helmet that covered the lower half of his head, as well as some of the rest of the armor.<ref name="Synara's Score" /> His armor had the Warbird logo painted on it. Leoz's left eye was covered with an eyepatch.<ref name="Kaz's Curse" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Leoz first appeared in "[[The Triple Dark]]," the second episode of ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|Season One]].<ref name="The Triple Dark" /> He was not identified until the [[Star Wars Resistance Season Two|season 2]] episode "[[Kaz's Curse]]," where he was voiced by [[Steve Blum]].<ref name="Kaz's Curse" /> In the original script for "Kaz's Curse," the one who placed the curse on [[Kazuda Xiono]] was originally going to be a [[Kassk]] pirate named [[Vusk]] until the crew opted to use Leoz instead.<ref name="Original Script">{{SW|url=news/buckets-list-extra-kazs-curse-star-wars-resistance|text=Bucket's List Extra: 4 Fun Facts from "Kaz's Curse" - ''Star Wars Resistance''}}</ref>

